            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0588" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1028</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Appointed Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 884</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In a note addressed by Lord Curzon to the
                    United States Ambassador in London on September 13th,<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d455-f1"/> relative to the present negotiations for affording
                    financial assistance to Liberia, a copy of which you have no doubt received from
                    Mr. Davis, it was stated in paragraph four of the specific points to which it
                    was thought desirable to call attention, that two outstanding British claims
                    against the Liberian Government had been traced, one of which, for £44.18.9 was
                    made by Messrs. Wayland and Son, Limited, of Liverpool against the Liberian Post
                    Office.</p>
                <p>I have now received a communication from my Government stating that the Liberian
                    Government have informed the British Consulate <pb facs="0589" n="504"
                        xml:id="pg504"/> General at Monrovia that this obligation has now been
                    discharged.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For H. M. Ambassador)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C.
                            Lindsay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
